# B0 (no card opened): build the window image tp4-262k8-best-1 from the pushed tp4/262k8 commit. The profile named is the production default; nothing is baked as the image default
# (no C2_BAKE_DEFAULT_PROFILE), so the image default stays qwen_c2_profiles.json's c2-packed-tp4. THE TAG MUST BE FRESH: the build step skips a tag that already exists.
# PRECONDITION: the 262k stage-1 card evidence (the ordered-writer record and the packed-any record at capacity 262,144) is committed on this branch with its re-pinned constants, or the
# 8x262k profiles do not attach (packed_any_admission refuses a served capacity without a PASS section). No privileged builder container may be up (a refused E1w was exactly that).
# READ: the build log's provenance report with no problem line, the closure checks pass, the image id printed. Never run it during a timing job. Duration (estimate): 20-60 min. Stop rule: a build or provenance failure stops the window.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/262k8 eight-seat 262k development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/262k8 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/262k8 commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=build
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-262k8-best-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4
